'''Ovissians''' were a [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] with a bipedal figure and two pairs of horns. A population of Ovissians inhabited the [[planet]] [[Krystar]] by the [[time]] of the [[Clone Wars]]. The Ovissian [[Boolio]], a [[Mining|mine]] [[overseer]] on the [[Sinta Glacier]] [[Water|ice]] [[asteroid]], was a secret associate of the [[Resistance]] during its [[First Order-Resistance War|war]] against the [[First Order]].

==Biology and appearance==
The Ovissian [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] had a bipedal form and a rounded face. Their skin could be [[Color|green]]<ref name="TROS VD" /> or light<ref name="Battlefront II" /> in color. Their [[blood]] was rich in [[copper]]. The species' [[eye]] color ranged from brown<ref name="TROS VD" /> to black.<ref name="Battlefront II" /> Ovissians could also have [[hair]], including facial hair, in colors such as black or red.<ref name="Battle Tales 3" />

Ovissians had two pairs of polycerate horns on their heads&mdash;the greater pair extended from the sides of the head, while the lesser horns jutted from the mandible. Members of the species could grow to at least 1.78 [[meter]]s in height.<ref name="TROS VD" />

==Society and culture==
The population of Ovissians that resided on the [[planet]] [[Krystar]] were led by a [[regent]], who ruled from a [[Krystar palace|palace]].<ref name="Battle Tales 3" /> Ovissians could speak [[Galactic Basic Standard]].<ref name="TROS">{{Film|IX}}</ref>

==History==
[[File:QuebAndTrandoshan-TCWBattleTales3.jpg|thumb|left|230px|Regent Queb dealt with the Separatists and Trandoshan hunters during the Clone Wars.]]
In [[22 BBY]],<ref name="BT3 Date">[[Star Wars Adventures: The Clone Wars – Battle Tales 3|''Star Wars Adventures: The Clone Wars – Battle Tales'' 3]] places the [[Mission on Krystar|mission to Krystar]] during the [[Clone Wars]] and prior to the [[siege of Hisseen]], which [[Star Wars Adventures: The Clone Wars – Battle Tales 1|''Star Wars Adventures: The Clone Wars – Battle Tales'' 1]] establishes is prior to the [[Battle of Christophsis]]. Since the [[First Battle of Geonosis|beginning]] of the Clone Wars and the Battle of [[Christophsis]] are dated to [[22 BBY]] by ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'', the mission to [[Krystar]], and the appearance of Ovissians, must take place in that [[Standard year|year]].</ref> during the [[Clone Wars]], a population of Ovissians resided on the planet Krystar, ruled by the Ovissian regent [[Queb]] and represented in the [[Galactic Republic]] by [[Vishar Koss]]. Queb secretly worked with the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]], keeping Republic [[clone trooper]]s [[prisoner]] on Krystar, who he sold to a [[Unidentified Trandoshan hunter (Krystar)|Trandoshan hunter]]. After Koss discovered the [[Queb's compound|compound]] where Queb kept the [[trooper]]s, she contacted her associate [[Senator]] [[Padmé Amidala Naberrie|Padmé Amidala]], leading to a Republic [[Mission on Krystar|mission]] where the [[Cloning|clones]] were rescued and Queb was taken into custody.<ref name="Battle Tales 3" />

In around [[28 ABY]],<ref name="TROKR Date">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary]]'' states that the [[Destruction of the Jedi Temple|destruction]] of [[Luke Skywalker]]'s [[Jedi Temple of Luke Skywalker|Jedi temple]] occurred six [[Standard year|years]] before the [[Hosnian Cataclysm|Starkiller Incident]]. Since ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' dates the Starkiller Incident to [[34 ABY]], and the events of [[The Rise of Kylo Ren 3|''The Rise of Kylo Ren'' 3]] are set immediately after the temple's destruction, it can be deduced that the events of ''The Rise of Kylo Ren'' 3 are set around [[28 ABY]].</ref> an Ovissian was present at a [[cantina]] on the [[Mid Rim Territories|Mid Rim]] astronomical object [[Varnak]] when [[Ben Solo]], former [[Jedi]] [[Padawan]] of [[Jedi Master]] [[Luke Skywalker]], met with "[[Ren (human)|Ren]]," the leader of the [[Dark side of the Force|dark side]] organization known as the [[Knights of Ren]].<ref name="The Rise of Kylo Ren 3">[[The Rise of Kylo Ren 3|''The Rise of Kylo Ren'' 3]]</ref>

An Ovissian served as the [[Unidentified Ovissian headmaster|headmaster]] of a [[Unidentified school (Merokia)|school]] on the [[desert]] [[planet]] [[Merokia]]. The headmaster came into conflict with the student [[Karr Nuq Sin]], believing that his [[Force vision]]s were simply headaches.<ref name="Force Collector" />

[[File:Finn-Boolio.png|thumb|right|270px|Boolio provides the Resistance with First Order intelligence.]]
The Ovissian [[Boolio]], who hailed from the astronomical object [[Sinta IV]], worked as a [[Mining|mine]] [[overseer]] on the [[Sinta Glacier]], a large [[Water|ice]] [[asteroid]] that [[orbit]]ed the [[Sinta|same]] [[star]].<ref name="TROS VD" /> By [[35 ABY]],<ref name="TROS Date">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary]]'' places the events of [[Star Wars: Episode IX The Rise of Skywalker|''Star Wars'': Episode IX ''The Rise of Skywalker'']] one [[Standard year|year]] after the [[Hosnian Cataclysm]]. As the Hosnian Cataclysm is dated to [[34 ABY]] by ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'', the events of ''The Rise of Skywalker'' take place in [[35 ABY]].</ref> Boolio had secretly become an affiliate of the Resistance, covertly supplying the group with surplus materials. After receiving an anonymous message from an [[Armitage Hux|officer]] of the First Order, Boolio contacted the Resistance, who initiated a [[Mission to Sinta Glacier Colony|mission]] to retrieve the information.<ref name="TROS VD" /> However, Boolio was discovered by the First Order, who had the Ovissian [[Death|executed]].<ref name="TROS" />

==Behind the scenes==
Ovissians were created for the [[2019]] film [[Star Wars: Episode IX The Rise of Skywalker|''Star Wars'': Episode IX ''The Rise of Skywalker'']],<ref name="TROS" /> but first appeared in the novel ''[[Force Collector]]'', written by [[Kevin Shinick]].<ref name="Force Collector" />

